## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage-touching" test suite** — every production method is invoked (giving you 95%+ line coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if every method returns garbage or corrupts data.

---

### Severity-Ranked Findings

| # | Severity | Anti-Pattern | Test(s) |
|---|----------|--------------|---------|
| 1 | 🔴 Critical | **Assertion-free test** | `AddProduct_Works`, `UpdatePrice_Works`, `RemoveProduct_Works`, `GetProductCount_Works`, `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`, `ImportFromCsv_Works` |
| 2 | 🔴 Critical | **Trivial assertion (IsNotNull only)** | `GetProduct_Works`, `SearchProducts_Works`, `GetAllProducts_Works`, `ExportToCsv_Works` |
| 3 | 🟠 High | **No negative/edge-case path** | All tests — missing `KeyNotFoundException` for `UpdatePrice` on missing SKU, empty search, empty CSV |
| 4 | 🟡 Medium | **No state-transition verification** | `RemoveProduct_Works` never checks the item is gone; `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` never checks new prices |

---

### Concrete Fixes

**1. `AddProduct_Works` → verify the product is retrievable:**
```csharp
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved.Price);
```

**2. `GetProduct_Works` → assert on returned values, not just non-null:**
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result!.Sku);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
```

**3. `UpdatePrice_Works` → verify the price actually changed:**
```csharp
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**4. `RemoveProduct_Works` → confirm deletion:**
```csharp
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**5. `SearchProducts_Works` → assert count and content:**
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);
```

**6. `GetProductCount_Works` → assert the count value:**
```csharp
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**7. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` → verify discounted prices:**
